

                           Qandy PC DOS:
                           Disk Operating System (dos4.js)
                           <host> API


     —————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
           QDOS User Commands - input into Qandy Console to execute disk operations:
     —————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————      

                   fdisk — displays disk information and installs Qandy files 

                     dir — display directory, switches: -h hidden files,
                           -t timestamps, -n sort names, -e sort exts,
                           -s sort sizes

                    list — display list of files, can also use ls
                    
              mkdir name — make a <directory> named name, can also use 'md'
                   
              chdir name — change working directory, '..' to go back a directory,
                           '.' for root, no name to display current directory, can
                           also use 'cd'
                           
              rmdir name — remove (delete) directory named name, can also use 'rd'   
               
             qpaste file — paste clipboard contents into file on localStorage
       
       rename src = dest — rename file, can also use ren
       
            mount device — mounts a device, 'harddrive' for File Access API or 
                           'local' for localStorage
                           
             exists file — returns true if file exists

             

        * if filename starts with an underline, it is considered "hidden"
       ** if filename ends with an explainion mark, it is consdiered "write protected"              



     —————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————
                                    VARIABLES:
     —————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

                   name — Name of file, maximum length 255 bytes, allowed
                          characters: A–Z, a–z, 0–9, space (leading/trailing
                          trimmed), minus, underscore, dot (but not first
                          character), parentheses, plus, and equals: -_.()+= 
                       
                   data — plain UTF‑8 text, use base64 for binary data, dos.js
               load file — displays contents of file, 'load dir.sys' for raw directory 
               
            mount device — mounts a device, 'harddrive' for File Access API or 
                           'local' for localStorage
                           
             exists file — returns true if file exists

             

        * if filename starts with an underline, it is considered "hidden"
       ** if filename ends with an explainion mark, it is consdiered "write protected"              
             

             
     ————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————— 
               Advanced DOS API function calls - can only run on HOST machine
     —————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————————

         DOS=true/false — set to true if DOS is enabled, all DOS functions should
                          be inside "if (DOS) {}" checks    
 
       dosMount(device) — sets the active device to access
      
          DEVICE="name" — local var for active device
      
        dosBackup(data) — formats active device with JSON strong, if data is omitted
                          returns JSON string with contents of device for backup
     
     dosSave(file,data) — saves data as filename to active device, if filename
                          begins with > (">filename") append data to existing file,
                          do not allow append to filenames that start with ! as
                          they are write-protected.

          dosLoad(file) — returns contents of filename from active device as string,
                          file "dir.txt" returns list of files serperated by new
                          lines, file "dir.sys" returns raw directory information.
                          
    dosCopy(file, dest) — copies file into clipboard for dosPaste command, 
                          if dest is provided it also copies the file into
                          the dest file, returns error if dest already exists
                          
         dosPaste(dest) — pastes the clipboard contents into dest, will append
                          the data to existing dest if dest starts with ">" character,
                          otherwise returns error if file already exists.

      dosRetrieve(file) — Retrieve file from localStorage, used to send to <guest>
      
         dosStash(file) — Stash a file from the <guest> to localStorage
            
   dosRename(file,dest) — renames file to dest

        dosDelete(file) — deletes filename from active device 

        dosExists(file) — returns true if filename exists      


